<<<
termly, a. & adv. The word has been so far displaced by terminal(ly) that there is now a tinge of affectation in its use. The analogy of daily, weekly, monthly, yearly, fails because term, unlike day &c., is of Latin origin.
===
**termly,** a. & adv. The word has been so far displaced by *terminal(ly)* that there is now a tinge of affectation in its use. The analogy of *daily, weekly, monthly, yearly,* fails because *term*, unlike *day* &c., is of Latin origin.
>>>

